# Structural syllogism ratchet, migrated from tests/syllogism.sh.
# The class names are fresh on every run: the engine cannot pass by lexical
# lookup. `${A}`, `${B}`, `${C}` and `${D}` are test-engine variables.

[test universal_syllogism]
!set PARROT0_BASE=
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!random A 5
!random B 5
!random C 5
!random D 5
!timeout 2

> if all ${A}s are ${B}s and all ${B}s are ${C}s, are all ${A}s ${C}s?
< Yes.

> all ${A}s are ${B}s. all ${B}s are ${C}s. are all ${A}s ${C}s?
< Yes.

> if all ${A}s are ${B}s and all ${D}s are ${C}s, are all ${A}s ${C}s?
< No.

> if all ${A}s are ${B}s and zorb is a ${A}, is zorb a ${B}?
< Yes.

> if all ${A}s are ${B}s, and some ${B}s are ${C}s, but no ${C}s are ${A}s, can we conclude anything about the relationship between ${A}s and ${C}s?
< Those classes do not overlap -- the explicit no-overlap premise states that directly.

# gen384: il muro NOMINA dove si e' fermato invece di tacere. La premessa parla
# di ${D}, la domanda di ${C}: il legame non c'e', e parrot0 lo dice indicando il
# termine che non aggancia niente. L'attesa vecchia — il muro cieco — era la
# risposta peggiore delle due, non un contratto da difendere.
> if all ${A}s are ${B}s, and some ${B}s are ${C}s, but no ${C}s are ${D}s, can we conclude anything about the relationship between ${A}s and ${C}s?
<~ I don't know about

> if all ${A}s are ${B}s and all ${B}s are ${C}s, are all ${A}s ${C}s?
< Yes.
> what do you know about ${A}?
<~ I don't know anything about ${A}
> how many facts do you know?
<~ I know
